# The SQLite database is a CACHE, never the store of record. It is rebuilt
# from the committed plain-text data with `python3 -m osrs_index restore`.
# Measured over 14 daily commits: SQLite packs to 3.10 MiB against 1.00 MiB
# for the equivalent NDJSON, and a binary diff is unreviewable either way.
data/*.sqlite3
data/*.sqlite3-wal
data/*.sqlite3-shm

# data/bars/, data/history/ and data/items.json ARE committed on purpose:
# they are what the site fetches and what makes the index reproducible.

# Generated by `publish`; rebuilt on every CI run and served from the Pages
# artifact rather than from the repo.
site/data/

*.csv

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
